 ROE near 81% (asset-light, high-leverage financial model, though ROIC/net-debt-to-EBITDA are not meaningfully computable for this business type). FCF growth of 25% and a 36% FCF margin, combined with zero reported debt and $10B cash, indicate a fortress balance sheet funding aggressive buybacks (-5.8% dilution YoY) and ~9% shareholder yield.","technical_read":"Price is below both the 20- and 50-day moving averages and marginally below the 200-day (-0.4%), with RSI at 43 signaling neutral-to-weak momentum, though MACD remains slightly positive and the 50-day is still above the 200-day (intact longer-term uptrend). The stock is down 14% from its 52-week high and -11% over 3 months despite a flattish 12-month return, suggesting a corrective phase within a longer uptrend rather than a confirmed breakdown.","market_expectation":"The 11x P/E (0th percentile of 5-year history) and 0.5 PEG, paired with flat-to-negative recent momentum, imply the market is pricing stagnation or deterioration in Ameriprise's earnings power, not crediting the margin expansion and FCF growth actually occurring.","what_market_misses":["Reality (60) is running well ahead of what's priced (34), a 26-point expectations gap that isn't closing.","Margin expansion (+170bps operating margin YoY) and 25% FCF growth are occurring faster than the multiple reflects.","Financials sector rotation is positive (+55) but this specific name hasn't participated, leaving room to catch up if rotation persists.","Aggressive buybacks (-5.8% share count) at a depressed multiple are quietly compounding per-share value that backward-looking price action doesn't capture."],"catalysts":["Next quarterly earnings report (~90 days after the 2026-10-30 filing) could reset market perception of margin trajectory.","Continued capital rotation into Financials sector (currently +55 score) could pull valuation higher.","Technical stabilization above the 200-day average (currently -0.4% below) could trigger momentum-driven buying."